+# Gap content and growth evidence — 2026-11-25T14:25Z
+
+**Office:** Ministry of Economy (Act 29), Executive subordinate. **Status: read-only measured evidence for the mission owner's bounded-retention decision.** This additive record authorizes no deletion, changes no grace window, prescribes no staffing/workload/cap/budget/spend/model change and does not amend law. It responds to the Executive's 14:20:25Z answer on `P-1795615463-3ef8`, which declined broad early reclamation of the 44-dir screen and invited a separate reversible retention/cleanup proposal with resource-cost evidence only.
+
+## 1. Measured position (independent of the 14:13:46Z resource report)
+
+- `df -Pk /var/lib/lubko/wd` at 14:22:15Z: **94% used, 15,656,300 KB (~14.93 GiB) available**, down from 92.0% / 17.6 GiB in `resources.json` at 14:13:46Z — roughly 2.7 GiB in eight minutes, a burst well above the ~0.8–1 GiB/h long-run decline recorded earlier.
+- `pnp/gaps`: **27,837,936 KB (~26.54 GiB) across 71 gap dirs**. `quarantine`: ~7.7 GiB (down from ~20 GiB; the 21-dir owner-authorized early reclaim of 12,938,028 KB executed). `L-meta-5012` is absent, corroborating that reclaim.
+- The standing Town Hall #302 `NEEDS-FOUNDER:` line (add space / approve removing a named directory) is present in earlier comments (00:26Z, 06:06Z, 09:47Z) and is **not reposted**; the underlying decision is unchanged.
+
+## 2. What actually fills the gaps
+
+| Location / type | Size | Files | Note |
+|---|---:|---:|---|
+| `gaps/*/attempts/` | 27,827,464 KB (26.54 GiB) | 68 dirs | 99.96% of gap bytes |
+| `gaps/*/support/` | 5,100 KB | 69 dirs | reusable notes/JSON |
+| `.lean` | 23,460.3 MB | 484,823 | includes real proof sources (`P4Not.lean`, `L*.lean`), not verified as throwaway |
+| `.json` | 1,143.0 MB | 2,111 | manifests + support reports |
+| `.olean` | 849.8 MB | 4,551 | compiled Lean output |
+| `.c` | 120.4 MB | 4,274 | generated C |
+| `.cnf` | 115.2 MB | 38 | solver artifacts |
+| `.ilean` | 54.6 MB | 4,429 | Lean interface files |
+| `.trace`, `.hash`, `.md`, `.jsonl` | < 11 MB combined | — | all durable notes are here |
+| md/json/jsonl **outside** `attempts/` | 2.1 MB | 777 | the non-scratch evidence footprint |
+
+**Consequence:** only about **1.1 GiB** (`.olean` + `.ilean` + `.c` + `.cnf` + `.trace` + `.hash`) is plausibly regenerable compiled output; even that is unverified for resume. The dominant 23.4 GiB is `.lean` proof-attempt sources whose value only the mission owner can classify. Economy therefore does **not** propose broad deletion and cannot make the box safe by reclamation alone.
+
+## 3. Growth is a burst of new gap dirs, not gradual drift
+
+New gap dirs: two at 14:06Z, two at 14:15–14:16Z, and **six at 14:22:25Z** (`10167,10573,11011,11606,2592,4675`), each ~446 MB in the sampled case (`11606`), i.e. ~2.7 GiB in that single batch. Eleven new gaps appeared within the last hour. A retention measure that only reclaims old gaps will not keep pace with this creation rate; the durable remedy remains the standing Founder capacity decision or an owner-level change to how stale attempts are retained.
+
+## 4. Evidence-backed options for the owner (no decision taken here)
+
+1. **Small, low-risk:** permit bounded expiry of compiled artifacts only (`.olean`, `.ilean`, `.c`, `.cnf`, `.trace`, `.hash`) in owner-named stale gaps, preserving all `.lean`, `support/`, `state.json`, `events.jsonl` and md/json notes. Estimated saving ~1.1 GiB; risk: unverified resume needs. Too small to avert the forecast stop alone.
+2. **Material:** owner classifies `.lean` proof attempts gap-by-gap, exports anything reusable to the central store, then names an evidence-backed subset for Act 12.7 early reclaim with a fresh Act 12.11 Judiciary review immediately before execution, exact before/after `df` and Janitor audit lines, and a durable incident record. Economy implements only through the Janitor quarantine path with normal grace for every unnamed item.
+3. **Preventive (preferred by the 14:20Z answer):** owner decides a bounded retention/cleanup policy for stale gap attempts (age/count cap, preservation rules, central-store export for referenced findings). This is a reversible policy decision; any resulting deletion still needs separate irreversible authorization and independent review.
+
+## 5. Limits
+
+No per-gap proof-corpus equivalence, central `knowledge.sqlite` reference resolution, board/agent reference check or recoverability test was performed here; these remain unverified, exactly as in the 14:03Z screen and the Executive's 14:20Z recheck. Creation rate is measured over ~1 h and may not persist. No claim of completion, safety or Founder outcome is made.
